## Picking this back up

```bash
cd [path/to/repo]
git fetch --all
git for-each-ref --sort=-committerdate --format='%(committerdate:short)  %(refname:short)' refs/remotes/ | head -5
git log --oneline [branch]..origin/[newest]   # what landed while away
```

Then read, in order: [the shortest path to being productive again — the getting-started doc, the specs
index, the most relevant ADR. Point at durable committed docs, not at this file.]
